                                            // single, un-retried attempt. marketplace_listings' create
                                            // rule only requires isRealAccount() (a real, non-anonymous
                                            // Firebase Auth session) — the same condition app-patch-v31.js
                                            // already documented as racy on this app (an anonymous
                                            // fallback session and/or a stale ID token can still be
                                            // attached to a request for a moment even though the person
                                            // is genuinely logged in). When that race is lost the write
                                            // is denied with exactly "Missing or insufficient
                                            // permissions" — and the catch below used to just log a
                                            // console.warn and silently carry on as if the listing had
                                            // saved, so the media upload the person just watched
                                            // "succeed" never actually reached Firestore at all: fine on
                                            // this device until reload, invisible on every other one.
                                            // Mirrors the exact token-refresh-then-retry-once pattern
